WEBVTT

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:01.323 line:86%
Hi everyone,

00:00:01.363 --> 00:00:02.984 line:86%
my name is Ramon and today I'll

00:00:03.024 --> 00:00:04.291 line:86%
show you everything about

00:00:04.331 --> 00:00:05.320 line:86%
Vizai Render.

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:07.092 line:86%
I'll start with the whole

00:00:07.132 --> 00:00:09.360 line:86%
interface and what each function

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.030 line:86%
does in your project.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:12.078 line:86%
Right after that,

00:00:12.118 --> 00:00:13.811 line:86%
we'll generate some images of

00:00:13.851 --> 00:00:15.660 line:86%
a residential facade project,

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.814 line:86%
where I'll walk you step by step

00:00:17.854 --> 00:00:19.466 line:86%
through your first render

00:00:19.506 --> 00:00:21.596 line:86%
and explain how to create new image

00:00:21.636 --> 00:00:22.336 line:86%
variations.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:23.353 line:86%
To start,

00:00:23.393 --> 00:00:25.888 line:86%
I'll open Vizai and show you all

00:00:25.928 --> 00:00:27.393 line:86%
6 tabs available in

00:00:27.433 --> 00:00:28.731 line:86%
the plugin interface,

00:00:28.771 --> 00:00:30.446 line:86%
each one for a different stage

00:00:30.486 --> 00:00:31.400 line:86%
of your project.

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:33.461 line:86%
We have the Scenes,

00:00:33.501 --> 00:00:34.139 line:86%
Studio,

00:00:34.179 --> 00:00:36.020 line:86%
Video and 360 tabs,

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:39.259 line:86%
Blocks, and the History tab with every

00:00:39.299 --> 00:00:40.520 line:86%
image you generated.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.542 line:86%
There's also your profile tab,

00:00:43.582 --> 00:00:45.219 line:86%
where you can see all

00:00:45.259 --> 00:00:46.430 line:86%
your available

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:47.135 line:86%
credits,

00:00:47.175 --> 00:00:49.483 line:86%
and the subscription button

00:00:49.523 --> 00:00:51.870 line:86%
where you can buy a plan or

00:00:51.920 --> 00:00:53.550 line:86%
buy extra credits without

00:00:53.590 --> 00:00:54.860 line:86%
leaving the plugin.

00:00:59.460 --> 00:01:01.510 line:86%
Let me start with the Scenes tab.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:03.218 line:86%
It's where you set up all

00:01:03.258 --> 00:01:06.060 line:86%
your scenes before generating any image.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:09.240 line:86%
Here you choose scene lighting,

00:01:09.531 --> 00:01:10.340 line:86%
framing,

00:01:10.380 --> 00:01:11.760 line:86%
focal length,

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:14.230 line:86%
rule of thirds and two-point

00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:15.143 line:86%
perspective,

00:01:15.183 --> 00:01:17.390 line:86%
then save your scene with all

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:18.940 line:86%
the settings you picked.

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:39.965 line:86%
This tab has two options I'll

00:01:40.005 --> 00:01:41.835 line:86%
cover in a separate video,

00:01:41.875 --> 00:01:42.482 line:86%
which are

00:01:42.522 --> 00:01:44.912 line:86%
the mirror reflection and fake light

00:01:44.952 --> 00:01:45.652 line:86%
features.

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:48.160 line:86%
Now let's open a reference project,

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:50.122 line:86%
so I can show you the Studio tab

00:01:50.162 --> 00:01:51.940 line:86%
and start rendering for real.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:55.759 line:86%
With the project open,

00:01:55.799 --> 00:01:57.400 line:86%
I'll adjust a few settings

00:01:57.440 --> 00:01:58.700 line:86%
and save our scene.

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:01.206 line:86%
Then I'll set up the Studio tab

00:02:01.246 --> 00:02:03.440 line:86%
and generate our first image.

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:28.570 line:86%
When the render is done,

00:03:28.610 --> 00:03:30.493 line:86%
click Enlarge and a bigger view

00:03:30.533 --> 00:03:32.586 line:86%
opens so you can compare the before

00:03:32.626 --> 00:03:34.120 line:86%
and after of your image.

00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:47.839 line:86%
With the image finished,

00:03:47.879 --> 00:03:49.980 line:86%
let me show you the Edit tab.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:51.797 line:86%
There you can create variations

00:03:51.837 --> 00:03:52.630 line:86%
of your image.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:54.664 line:86%
You can use the selection brush

00:03:54.704 --> 00:03:56.687 line:86%
to add or remove an object from

00:03:56.727 --> 00:03:57.427 line:86%
the scene.

00:03:57.600 --> 00:03:59.857 line:86%
You can also crop the image or

00:03:59.897 --> 00:04:02.270 line:86%
make small adjustments to white

00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:03.450 line:86%
balance and color.

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:04.893 line:86%
Now I'll generate a few

00:04:04.933 --> 00:04:06.887 line:86%
variations and make small tweaks

00:04:06.927 --> 00:04:07.560 line:86%
so you can

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:08.800 line:86%
see how it works.

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:56.568 line:86%
Every image you generate shows

00:04:56.608 --> 00:04:57.546 line:86%
up here on the side,

00:04:57.586 --> 00:04:58.419 line:86%
in the History.

00:04:58.660 --> 00:05:00.198 line:86%
From there just save them

00:05:00.238 --> 00:05:02.080 line:86%
to your computer one by one.

00:05:02.480 --> 00:05:04.424 line:86%
Careful not to forget to save them.

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:05.780 line:86%
Oh, one more thing.

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:07.932 line:86%
In the Edit tab you can create

00:05:07.972 --> 00:05:10.155 line:86%
new views of your project based

00:05:10.195 --> 00:05:12.160 line:86%
on that first image you generated.

00:05:12.200 --> 00:05:13.590 line:86%
That way it keeps the same

00:05:13.630 --> 00:05:14.745 line:86%
lighting and the same

00:05:14.785 --> 00:05:15.507 line:86%
surroundings.

00:05:15.640 --> 00:05:17.266 line:86%
But if you want a much more

00:05:17.306 --> 00:05:18.192 line:86%
specific image,

00:05:18.232 --> 00:05:20.105 line:86%
you'll have to change the scene

00:05:20.145 --> 00:05:23.145 line:86%
in SketchUp and render another image.

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:07.114 line:86%
And for closer shots of details,

00:06:07.154 --> 00:06:08.641 line:86%
just type close-up like

00:06:08.681 --> 00:06:10.130 line:86%
in this example.

00:07:37.190 --> 00:07:38.993 line:86%
And here are all the images we

00:07:39.033 --> 00:07:40.200 line:86%
generated together.

00:07:40.250 --> 00:07:42.076 line:86%
Now I'll open another project

00:07:42.116 --> 00:07:44.710 line:86%
to show how it works for interiors too.

00:07:44.930 --> 00:07:45.597 line:86%
As you saw,

00:07:45.637 --> 00:07:46.730 line:86%
it's really fast.

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:48.962 line:86%
Imagine making all these images

00:07:49.002 --> 00:07:49.702 line:86%
in V-Ray.

00:07:56.230 --> 00:07:57.888 line:86%
With the interior project it's

00:07:57.928 --> 00:07:58.890 line:86%
the same process.

00:07:59.490 --> 00:08:00.685 line:86%
Adjust the scene,

00:08:00.725 --> 00:08:03.050 line:86%
set the project type and render.

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:04.661 line:86%
Then just create the image

00:08:04.701 --> 00:08:06.250 line:86%
variations in the Edit tab.

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:08.384 line:86%
And it's very important to check

00:08:08.424 --> 00:08:09.424 line:86%
this first option.

00:08:09.570 --> 00:08:10.200 line:86%
With it on,

00:08:10.240 --> 00:08:12.090 line:86%
all the materials in your scene

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:13.370 line:86%
stay clearly visible,

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:14.090 line:86%
which helps

00:08:14.130 --> 00:08:16.210 line:86%
the AI understand them better.

00:09:26.980 --> 00:09:28.766 line:86%
Remember that the new views

00:09:28.806 --> 00:09:30.660 line:86%
created here in the Edit tab

00:09:30.700 --> 00:09:33.220 line:86%
are built from a reference image.

00:09:33.380 --> 00:09:34.462 line:86%
Like in this example,

00:09:34.502 --> 00:09:36.011 line:86%
the first image we generated,

00:09:36.051 --> 00:09:37.162 line:86%
here in the History.

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:39.745 line:86%
Now if you want a new side view

00:09:39.785 --> 00:09:41.930 line:86%
that isn't visible here, you'll

00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:44.083 line:86%
have to move the camera inside

00:09:44.123 --> 00:09:45.980 line:86%
SketchUp and render again.

00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:47.661 line:86%
Because the AI can't see

00:09:47.701 --> 00:09:48.782 line:86%
your whole project,

00:09:48.822 --> 00:09:50.310 line:86%
only what has already been

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:51.560 line:86%
rendered.

00:11:48.730 --> 00:11:49.910 line:86%
Now take a look at all

00:11:49.950 --> 00:11:51.980 line:86%
the images generated here in Vizai.

00:11:52.030 --> 00:11:53.455 line:86%
In the next video I'll show

00:11:53.495 --> 00:11:55.005 line:86%
you how to create every kind

00:11:55.045 --> 00:11:56.640 line:86%
of mirror reflection and how

00:11:56.690 --> 00:11:58.253 line:86%
to make fake light inside

00:11:58.293 --> 00:11:58.990 line:86%
SketchUp.

00:11:59.030 --> 00:12:00.570 line:86%
See you in the next video.

